00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:52.230
I mean, this is affecting every segment, every
segment of society right now in the last bit

00:08:52.230 --> 00:08:53.400
of time we have.

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:58.110
Is there any thing we have not talked about
either in terms of programs or in terms of

00:08:58.110 --> 00:09:03.100
what individuals can or should be doing that
you think is important for people to know?

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:06.880
So I did want to talk briefly about the programs
that are available because there have been

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:10.870
some changes to the program since they were
initially announced.

00:09:10.870 --> 00:09:16.420
So the first program that's available is the
Economic Injury Disaster Loan Grant.

00:09:16.420 --> 00:09:22.290
So the bill said and the Small Business Administration
initially said that these were going to be

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:24.270
ten thousand dollar grants.

00:09:24.270 --> 00:09:26.280
So the SBA has now changed that.

00:09:26.280 --> 00:09:32.030
Now it's going to be one thousand dollar grant
per employee that the business employs up

00:09:32.030 --> 00:09:33.310
to ten thousand dollars.

00:09:33.310 --> 00:09:38.950
So you can imagine a lot of small businesses
may only be getting one or two thousand dollars.

00:09:38.950 --> 00:09:43.790
For example, those loans will be processed
in three days.

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:48.620
I don't know of any I mean, the link the application
has been up probably for a week and a half

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:49.620
or two weeks.

00:09:49.620 --> 00:09:51.100
And I don't know anyone who's gotten that.

00:09:51.100 --> 00:09:53.550
You can apply directly for that on the.

00:09:53.550 --> 00:09:55.100
A Web site if you Google SBA at 19.

00:09:55.100 --> 00:10:00.370
The second part of that is the paycheck protection
plan.

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:05.580
So that provides up to two and a half months
of payroll and it's a loan at 1 percent.

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:07.740
Now initially it was zero point five percent.

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:08.740
Now it's 1 percent.

00:10:08.740 --> 00:10:14.610
But the loan can be forgiven if 75 percent
or more of the proceeds of the loan are spent

00:10:14.610 --> 00:10:17.810
on payroll and your payroll does not decrease.

00:10:17.810 --> 00:10:21.220
And individual banks are the ones processing
those applications.

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:27.100
And then the third component are just ordinary
Small Business Administration loans are called

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:28.250
7 8 loans.

00:10:28.250 --> 00:10:33.540
And for new loans that are issued, the Small
Business Administration has pledged to pay

00:10:33.540 --> 00:10:37.080
six months of principal and interest on those
loans.

00:10:37.080 --> 00:10:41.870
And eventually you could get you could get
a loan that might be a two year loan.

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:46.930
And in the first six months, the that those
payments would be made for you and you would

00:10:46.930 --> 00:10:49.090
not need to make that up.

00:10:49.090 --> 00:10:50.090
Correct.

00:10:50.090 --> 00:10:57.500
So theoretically, you could pay the principal
back after six months minus the the principal

00:10:57.500 --> 00:11:01.470
payments that have already been made on your
behalf and you would not end up on any money

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:02.470
at all.

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:05.940
And of course, this is if you can actually
get the money disbursed, which seems to be

00:11:05.940 --> 00:11:08.410
a question mark around all of these programs
right now.

00:11:08.410 --> 00:11:09.410
Yeah.

00:11:09.410 --> 00:11:13.650
I mean, I'll tell you that the ordinary SBA
loans are a little easier to get just because

00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:15.190
banks make more money on that.

00:11:15.190 --> 00:11:17.670
The interest rates are substantially higher.

00:11:17.670 --> 00:11:19.410
The young people he loans.

00:11:19.410 --> 00:11:26.330
And so banks, although the difference with
the 7a loans is that the banks do assume some

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:27.480
risk on that.

00:11:27.480 --> 00:11:30.280
Usually from 25 to 50 percent or so.

00:11:30.280 --> 00:11:34.850
So banks may be more reluctant and probably
will be more reluctant to issue those loans

00:11:34.850 --> 00:11:36.680
right now.

00:11:36.680 --> 00:11:38.500
We will continue keeping an eye on it.

00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:42.871
And of course, as important as the small business
programs, the individual programs, unemployment

00:11:42.871 --> 00:11:49.410
and the twelve hundred dollar deposits, which
we are continuing to try to raise, the question

00:11:49.410 --> 00:11:51.620
marks around, but question marks certainly
remain.

